Third-party software and attribution

This repository does not contain the source code of any scanner it tests. The Dockerfiles install pinned
versions from the owners' own distribution channels:

- Cisco AI Defense Skill Scanner (cisco-ai-skill-scanner 2.3.0), Apache License 2.0
  https://github.com/cisco-ai-defense/skill-scanner
- NVIDIA SkillSpector (v2.13.0, commit 091a509b3d6ba8ff5be528966e1f43c2e68cf214), Apache License 2.0
  https://github.com/NVIDIA/skillspector
- Ollama (ollama/ollama image), MIT licence, https://github.com/ollama/ollama, and the model qwen2.5:7b, Apache License 2.0
  (Qwen team), used only for part 2
- matplotlib 3.11.2 (used only to draw the chart), matplotlib license
  https://matplotlib.org/
- Python 3.12 (Docker Official Image python:3.12-slim-bookworm), PSF License

The files under results/raw/ contain output produced by the scanners above when run on this repository's sample
Skills. Short excerpts of that output (rule names, titles, severities, matched lines of the samples) are included
for transparency and remain the work of their respective authors.

Framework names and identifiers (OWASP Top 10 for LLM Applications, OWASP Top 10 for Agentic Applications,
MITRE ATLAS, MITRE CWE, MITRE ATT&CK) belong to their owners and are used for reference only.
Mapping rule families to framework items is the author's judgement, not an official crosswalk.
